uid "98991be6-469f-529d-a233-ed9fc6b28adb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228001 #edb/ref 1080 "70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228001 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228001 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d9a16fb4-160b-585e-b61b-4270318e4528" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228002 #edb/ref 1080 "65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228002 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228002 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e66914e3-6386-5516-9016-9c264fa26d74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228003 #edb/ref 1080 "75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228003 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228003 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1f8bab44-dcf3-5c6a-8b9f-b82bc443967a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228878 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21452" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228878 #edb/ref 1071 "A discount of $14\\%$ is offered on all hiking boots. What is the sale price of a pair of boots originally priced at $\\[math]78?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228878 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "728d9eaf-6814-53b8-a3ac-f270c36c6e83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228878 #edb/ref 1074 "To find an amount that's $14\\%$ *less than* $\\[math]78,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\% - 14\\% = 86\\%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n86\\% = \\dfrac{86}{100} = 0.86\n$$\n\nSo, to find $86\\%$ of $\\[/math]78,$ we multiply $\\[math]78$ by $0.86{:}$\n\n$$\n0.86 \\cdot \\[/math]78 = \\[math]67.08\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sale price of the hiking boots is $\\[/math]67.08.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228888 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228888 #edb/ref 1071 "What number is $30\\%$ less than $120$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228888 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9701b962-e3cf-5374-8168-ac5cb575cc3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228888 #edb/ref 1074 "To find a number $30\\%$ *less than* $120,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\% - 30\\% = 70\\%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n70\\% = \\dfrac{70}{100} = 0.7\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $70\\%$ of $120,$ we multiply $120$ by $0.7{:}$\n\n$$\n0.7 \\cdot 120 = 84\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229115 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229115 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229115 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229115 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186508992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229115 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying a Percentage Decrease" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229115 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186228888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229115 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7a862a80-f316-5378-86aa-83ed3e9b6bef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229116 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229116 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229116 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186508983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229116 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying a Percentage Decrease: Word Problems" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229116 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186228878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229116 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e5d92700-fe95-5d2c-8b25-5b6e3af31411" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186229957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186229958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186229959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186230112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1045 "Applying Percentage Decreases" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186229957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229244 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "1a9c4969-4c9f-5278-998c-6785950a5786" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229595 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186227913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229595 #edb/ref 1069 "q-326539" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229595 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229595 #edb/ref 1071 "At a furniture store, all tables are discounted by $25%$ during a weekend sale. What is the sale price of a table that originally costs $$64?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229595 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e91b434e-4c59-5d04-a49f-266bb482b86c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229595 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229595 #edb/ref 1074 "To find an amount that's $25%$ *less than* $$64,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%-25%=75%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n75%=\\frac{75}{100}=0.75\n$$\n\nSo, to find $75%$ of $$64,$ we multiply $$64$ by $0.75:$\n\n$$\n0.75\\cdot $64=$48\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sale price of the table is $$48.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229610 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186227998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229610 #edb/ref 1069 "q-326970" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229610 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229610 #edb/ref 1071 "What number is $15%$ less than $80?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229610 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "262d10ee-b744-50f7-bae4-d67c2181ebd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229610 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229610 #edb/ref 1074 "To find a number $15%$ *less than* $80,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%-15%=85%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n85%=\\frac{85}{100}=0.85\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $85%$ of $80,$ we multiply $80$ by $0.85:$\n\n$$\n0.85\\cdot 80=68\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229957 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186230112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229957 #edb/ref 1061 576542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229957 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ca806adb-050c-5ff1-a4ef-dfc8b5522870" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229957 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186230172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229958 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186229959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229958 #edb/ref 1061 576543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229958 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "093facfa-02ce-5202-b8f2-cad4a28be065" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229958 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229959 #edb/ref 1061 576546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229959 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c173d97e-3f75-55b0-aaa0-06648d024013" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229959 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230112 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186229958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230112 #edb/ref 1061 615639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230112 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "00c48b44-448b-53d8-83aa-edd374737e54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230112 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186230242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230172 #edb/ref 1064 "In a previous lesson, we spent some time learning how to find a number that is a certain percentage *greater than* a given amount. This is known as finding a *percentage increase.*\n\nWe can apply similar reasoning to find a number that is a certain percentage *less than* a given amount. This corresponds to applying a **percentage decrease.**\n\nTo apply a percentage decrease, we do the following:\n\n1\\. Subtract the decrease from $100\\%.$\n\n2\\. Convert the result to a decimal multiplier.\n\n3\\. Find the product of the multiplier and the original number.\n\nLet's take a look at a worked example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230172 #edb/ref 1065 14352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230172 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "772e2725-79aa-5290-907e-aec1f5954fde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230172 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230242 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the following problem.\n\nWhat number is $20\\%$ less than $250?$\n\nThe key words here are \"$20\\%$ *less than.*\" This means we need to apply a percentage decrease, decreasing the original number by $20\\%.$\n\nTo solve this problem, we follow three steps.\n\n- **Step 1.** Subtract the decrease from $100\\%.$\n\nTo find a number $20\\%$ *less than* $250,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\% - 20\\% = 80\\%.\n$$\n\nThis means that our new number is $80\\%$ of $250.$\n\n- **Step 2.** Convert the result to a decimal multiplier.\n\nNow, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n80\\% = \\dfrac{80}{100} = 0.8\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the product of the multiplier and the original number.\n\nSo, to find a number that is $20\\%$ less than $250,$ we multiply $250$ by $0.8{:}$\n\n$$\n0.8 \\cdot 250 = 200\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $20\\%$ less than $250$ is $200.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230242 #edb/ref 1065 15088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230242 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8037f8a8-aa7d-5df9-ac6a-cb29948a4d2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230242 #edb/ref 1067 "A Worked Example" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508400 #edb/ref 1080 "$$74.25$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508400 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508400 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08ba13fe-1d0b-507b-85bb-128d69277956" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508413 #edb/ref 1080 "$$71.50$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508413 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508413 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0fc34084-dac6-528b-9bab-3c95b340ec89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508426 #edb/ref 1080 "$$73.00$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508426 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508426 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "18ab41f3-9e7c-549d-8e33-45a4d949c8b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508444 #