 17592186045417] [17592186508992 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508992 #edb/ref 1069 "q-327179" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508992 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508992 #edb/ref 1071 "What number is $15%$ less than $100$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508992 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8cd627c-513a-5c63-8a84-0bf723703c1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508992 #edb/ref 1074 "To find a number $15%$ *less than* $100,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%-15%=85%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n85%=\\frac{85}{100}=0.85\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $85%$ of $100,$ we multiply $100$ by $0.85:$\n\n$$\n0.85\\cdot 100=85\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
